{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added explicit `sigma_a ~ uniform(0, 100)` and `sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 100)` prior sampling statements. These correspond to the existing finite bounds on `sigma_a` and `sigma_y` and make the implicit proper uniform priors explicit for SafeStan's unique-prior requirement. No data fields were added or changed. The protected observation `y` remains a top-level data variable and is observed exactly once with a built-in distribution.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  int<lower=0> n_grade;
  int<lower=0> n_grade_pair;
  int<lower=0> n_pair;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=n_grade> grade;
  array[n_pair] int<lower=1, upper=n_grade_pair> grade_pair;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=n_pair> pair;
  vector[N] pre_test;
  vector[N] treatment;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  vector[n_pair] eta_a;
  vector[n_grade_pair] mu_a;
  vector<lower=0, upper=100>[n_grade_pair] sigma_a;
  vector<lower=0, upper=100>[n_grade] sigma_y;
  vector[n_grade] b;
  vector[n_grade] c;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[n_pair] a;
  vector<lower=0, upper=100>[N] sigma_y_hat;
  vector[N] y_hat;

  for (i in 1 : n_pair) {
    a[i] = 50 * mu_a[grade_pair[i]] + sigma_a[grade_pair[i]] * eta_a[i];
  }

  for (i in 1 : N) {
    y_hat[i] = a[pair[i]] + b[grade[i]] * treatment[i]
               + c[grade[i]] * pre_test[i];
    sigma_y_hat[i] = sigma_y[grade[i]];
  }
}
model {
  eta_a ~ normal(0, 1);
  mu_a ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_a ~ uniform(0, 100);
  sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 100);
  b ~ normal(0, 100);
  c ~ normal(0, 100);
  y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y_hat);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":3,"grade":[3,1,3],"grade_pair":[1,1,1,1],"n_grade":3,"n_grade_pair":1,"n_pair":4,"pair":[1,2,1],"pre_test":[6.433302222659345,3.6465725639912954,6.295509923344082],"treatment":[3.3008708151667303,3.3485402770191333,4.199699786180992],"y":[3.0,3.0,3.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
